   "response_text": "Fixed it. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**The cause:** In `invkit/pricing.py`, `bulk_discount()` gated the discount with a strictly-greater-than check:\n\n```python\nif quantity > BULK_THRESHOLD:   # BULK_THRESHOLD = 10\n```\n\nThat means 11+ qualified, but exactly 10 fell into the `return 0.0` branch \u2014 a textbook off-by-one against the \"10 or more units\" policy.\n\n**The fix:** flipped the operator to an inclusive comparison (one char, minimal diff, no test files touched):\n\n```python\nif quantity >= BULK_THRESHOLD:\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n- `bulk_discount` now yields `0.0` at 9 units, `5.0` at 10, and `5.5` at 11 on a $10 unit price \u2192 threshold behaviour matches the policy.\n- Existing suite: `4 passed`.\n- `BULK_THRESHOLD` was left as the single source of truth (DRY-kosher); no magic `10` smuggled in anywhere.\n\nDONE",
